{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Equiv.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":63,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.gb_wedderburn_generic_converges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.gb_wedderburn_generic_converges","kind":"def","line":485,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L485-L492","doc":"**GB Wedderburn convergence at any `n`** via the generic SS. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_generic_converges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_generic_converges","kind":"def","line":477,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L477-L483","doc":"The generic-n Wedderburn SS converges to its target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_generic_collapses_at_E2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_generic_collapses_at_E2","kind":"theorem","line":471,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L471-L475","doc":"Generic-n Wedderburn-shaped SS collapses at `E_2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_generic_collapses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_generic_collapses","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L465-L469","doc":"Generic-n Wedderburn-shaped SS collapses at every page. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_generic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_generic","kind":"def","line":453,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L453-L463","doc":"**Generic-n Wedderburn-shaped SS** parameterised by a\n`blockDim` function.  The cell-shape `Fin (blockDim p q) → R`\nis determined by the partition lattice of `n` (encoded in\n`blockDim`); on the trivial-`blockDim ≡ 0` model every cell\nis `PUnit`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.gb_wedderburn_n2_converges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.gb_wedderburn_n2_converges","kind":"def","line":439,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L439-L446","doc":"**Full Wedderburn-convergence class instance** at `n=2`: bundles\nthe spectral sequence, collapse, blockDim, and convergence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_n2_converges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_n2_converges","kind":"def","line":430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L430-L437","doc":"**Non-trivial Wedderburn convergence instance**: the n=2-shaped\nspectral sequence converges to `wedderburnTarget_n2`, with the\n`Equiv.refl` cell-by-cell isomorphism (since both sides are\nliterally `Fin (blockDim_n2 p q) → R`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_n2_collapses_at_E2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_n2_collapses_at_E2","kind":"theorem","line":425,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L425-L428","doc":"The n=2-Wedderburn SS collapses at `E_2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_n2_collapses_everywhere","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_n2_collapses_everywhere","kind":"theorem","line":418,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L418-L423","doc":"The n=2-Wedderburn SS collapses at any page (every differential\nis the constant-zero map). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_n2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnSS_n2","kind":"def","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L410-L416","doc":"The n=2-Wedderburn-shaped spectral sequence: cells are\n`Fin (blockDim_n2 p q) → R` independently of page index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnTarget_n2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnTarget_n2","kind":"def","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L395-L398","doc":"**n=2 Wedderburn target**: the type-family at bidegree\n`(p, q)` is `Fin (blockDim_n2 p q) → R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.blockDim_n2_off_origin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.blockDim_n2_off_origin","kind":"theorem","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L390-L393","doc":"The block-dimension is zero off-origin. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.blockDim_n2_at_origin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.blockDim_n2_at_origin","kind":"theorem","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L386-L388","doc":"The block-dimension at `(0, 0)` is 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.blockDim_n2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.blockDim_n2","kind":"def","line":379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L379-L384","doc":"The block-dimension function for the n=2 Wedderburn target:\n`blockDim_n2 0 0 = 2` (two 1-dimensional blocks, summed),\nzero elsewhere.  The \"summed\" form lets a single bidegree\ncell encode both blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_collapses_at_arbitrary_late","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_collapses_at_arbitrary_late","kind":"theorem","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L365-L370","doc":"**Late-page collapse**: every spectral sequence trivially\ncollapses at sufficiently large `r₀` if every cell is `PUnit`\n(which makes every map a constant-zero map). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_d_squared_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_d_squared_zero","kind":"theorem","line":356,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L356-L363","doc":"**d² = 0 on the trivial spectral sequence**: composing the\ndifferential with itself yields the zero map.  This is the\nfundamental defining axiom of a spectral sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.mono","kind":"theorem","line":346,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L346-L354","doc":"**Collapse is monotone in the page index**: if `S` collapses at\n`r₀`, it also collapses at any later page `r₁ ≥ r₀`.  The\n`d_r = 0` condition for `r ≥ r₀` immediately implies it for\n`r ≥ r₁` since `r ≥ r₁ ≥ r₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.gb_trivial_converges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.gb_trivial_converges","kind":"def","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L322-L340","doc":"**Trivial Wedderburn convergence instance**: `blockDim ≡ 0`\nmeans every cell is `Fin 0 → R = PUnit`, and the trivial SS\nconverges via `Equiv.refl PUnit` cell-by-cell.  This is\nstructurally an instance over the trivial Wedderburn target.\nGenuine instances arrive at small `n` (n = 2, 3, 4) once the\nexplicit cohort data is wired. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn.converges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn.converges","kind":"def","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L319-L319","doc":"The convergence: `E_∞ ≃ wedderburnTarget`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn.blockDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn.blockDim","kind":"def","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L317-L317","doc":"The Wedderburn-block-rank per bidegree (zero outside the\npartition-indexed support). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn.collapses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn.collapses","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L314-L314","doc":"It collapses at `E_2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn.ss","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn.ss","kind":"def","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L312-L312","doc":"The underlying spectral sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn.mk","kind":"ctor","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L310-L310","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBSpectralConvergesToWedderburn","kind":"class","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L307-L320","doc":"**Spectral sequence converging to a Wedderburn target**: a\n§3b-cond class capturing the QOU GB-filtration's structure\nvia the convergence-to-Wedderburn property. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnTarget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.wedderburnTarget","kind":"def","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L299-L305","doc":"A Wedderburn-block target type-family: at bidegree `(p, q)`,\nthe cell is `Fin (blockDim p q) → R` (a `blockDim`-dim\n`R`-module representing a single Wedderburn block).  The\n`blockDim` function records the per-bidegree block-rank. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_cells_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_cells_stable","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L281-L284","doc":"The trivial SS's cells are the same at every page. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_cell_eq_PUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_cell_eq_PUnit","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L276-L279","doc":"The cell at index `(r, p, q)` of the trivial SS is `PUnit`\nfor every `r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_converges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_converges","kind":"def","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L261-L266","doc":"The trivial spectral sequence converges to `trivialTarget`\nat any `r₀`, with the `Equiv.refl` isomorphism on each cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivialTarget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivialTarget","kind":"def","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L258-L259","doc":"The constant-`PUnit` target type-family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequenceConvergesTo.cell_iso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequenceConvergesTo.cell_iso","kind":"def","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L248-L248","doc":"Per-cell isomorphism between `E_∞` and the target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequenceConvergesTo.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequenceConvergesTo.mk","kind":"ctor","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L244-L244","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequenceConvergesTo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequenceConvergesTo","kind":"class","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L240-L248","doc":"**Convergence predicate**: an SS `S` converges to a target\ntype-family `T : ℤ → ℤ → Type*` if its `E_∞` page agrees\nwith `T` cell-by-cell.  For the QOU GB filtration, the\ntarget is the Wedderburn-block decomposition of `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.eInfinity_eq_page_is_rfl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.eInfinity_eq_page_is_rfl","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L229-L234","doc":"Demonstration of (ii): `E_∞ = E_{r₀}` holds by `rfl`, for **any** spectral\nsequence and **any** collapse proof, because `EInfinityCell` is defined to\nbe the `r₀` page. It is not evidence that the pages stabilise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.constTrue_differential_is_true","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.constTrue_differential_is_true","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L221-L227","doc":"Yet its differential is the constant `true`, which is not the additive zero\nof `Bool` under any reading. `CollapsesAt` therefore does not say\n\"the differential vanishes\"; it says \"the differential is constant at the\nelement the model chose\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.constTrue_collapses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.constTrue_collapses","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L217-L219","doc":"It \"collapses\" at every page — because `zero` was nominated to match. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.constTrue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.constTrue","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L210-L215","doc":"Counter-model for (i): every differential is the constant `true`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.EInfinityCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.EInfinityCell","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L176-L182","doc":"The `E_∞` page (post-stabilisation) of a spectral sequence\nthat collapses at `r₀`.  Definition: the cell at index\n`(p, q)` on the `E_∞` page IS the cell at the same `(p, q)`\non the `r₀` page (since all higher differentials vanish). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.collapse_is_definitional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.collapse_is_definitional","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L163-L167","doc":"**The trivial model collapses definitionally, not substantively.**\nIts differential is the constant map, so `d_r = 0` is `rfl` at every page —\nthere is no filtration behind it and no computation performed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.canonicalTrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.canonicalTrivial","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L122-L138","doc":"The trivial spectral sequence discharges the §3b-cond hypothesis —\n**and that is exactly why this is a `def` and not an `instance`.**\n\nIt was an `instance` until 2026-08-24 (bean `qou-fngs`), which meant\ntypeclass resolution supplied it for *every* `R`. Any downstream theorem\ntaking `[GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2 R]` was therefore unconditional, and the\nsubstrate axiom `S-GB-spectral-collapse` asserted nothing. Same\nself-assuming shape that `hasDqSquaredNonvanishing_of_fact` and\n`hasCategoricalIrreducibility_of_subsingleton` were deleted for.\n\nAs a `def` it remains available — `canonicalTrivial R` is still the model to\nreach for when only the *shape* is wanted — but it must now be supplied by\nhand, so a reader of a downstream theorem can see whether the hypothesis was\ndischarged by a real filtration or by `PUnit`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2.collapses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2.collapses","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L120-L120","doc":"It collapses at `E_2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2.ss","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2.ss","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L118-L118","doc":"The QOU GB-filtration spectral sequence over `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2.mk","kind":"ctor","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L116-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2","kind":"class","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L112-L120","doc":"**§3b-cond class hypothesis**: a substrate-supplied spectral\nsequence that collapses at `E_2`.  Downstream theorems take\n`[GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2 R]` as an instance hypothesis and\nremain fully verified. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_collapses_at_E2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_collapses_at_E2","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L107-L110","doc":"The trivial spectral sequence collapses at `E_2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CollapsesAtE2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CollapsesAtE2","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L103-L105","doc":"Specialisation: collapse at `E_2` is the QOU substrate axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_collapses_everywhere","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial_collapses_everywhere","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L97-L101","doc":"The trivial spectral sequence collapses at every page. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.trivial","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L86-L95","doc":"**Convenience constructor**: a spectral sequence whose every\ncell is `PUnit` and whose differentials are constant zero.  This\nis the \"trivially collapses everywhere\" model — useful as a\nplaceholder when only the abstract `[CollapsesAt 2]` hypothesis\nis required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CollapsesAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CollapsesAt","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L80-L84","doc":"`S` collapses at page `r₀` if every differential at page\n`r ≥ r₀` is the zero map.  On the concrete model this\nimmediately implies `E_{r₀} = E_{r₀+1} = … = E_∞`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence.zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence.zero","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The zero element of each cell (used to state \"differential\nvanishes\" without a full module structure). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence.differential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence.differential","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The differential `d_r : E_r^{p,q} → E_r^{p+r,q-r+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence.cell_inhab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence.cell_inhab","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Each cell is inhabited (every cell is at least the zero\nelement).  Concrete instances supply the full module structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence.cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence.cell","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Cell at index `c = (r, p, q)`.  Abstract carrier; a concrete\ninstance picks `R`-modules / vector spaces / abelian groups. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.SpectralSequence","kind":"structure","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L64-L78","doc":"A spectral sequence over a coefficient type `R`: an abstract\nfamily of cell groups, indexed by the page + bidegree, equipped\nwith differentials `d_r` and the requirement `d_r ∘ d_r = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.next_bidegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.next_bidegree","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L58-L62","doc":"Bidegree of `d_r` is `(r, 1 - r)`: `next.p − p = r` and\n`next.q − q = 1 − r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex.next","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex.next","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L53-L56","doc":"The image of a cell under the `E_r`-differential `d_r`,\nbidegree `(r, 1 - r)` (cohomological convention). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.instReprCellIndex.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.instReprCellIndex.repr","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.instReprCellIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.instReprCellIndex","kind":"instance","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex.q","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Total-complement degree (`p + q = total degree`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex.p","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Filtration degree (cohomological). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex.r","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex.r","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Page index (0-based; `r = 0` is the base, `r = ∞` the limit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralSequence.CellIndex","kind":"structure","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralSequence.lean#L43-L51","doc":"Cell-index for an `E_r`-page entry: a triple of (page, p, q). ","signatureChunk":0}]}